WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.900
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.630
This is a quick update on our plans with Two
Minute Papers.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.370
The more I look at our incredibly high quality
comments sections on YouTube or the community

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:17.470
efforts that started out on our subreddit,
the more I get the feeling that we should

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.550
strive to create a community platform around
the series.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:26.550
A platform for people who wish to learn, exchange
ideas, collaborate, and help each other.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.769
For instance, the Two Minute Papers Data project
has recently started.

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:35.980
The initial idea is that there would be a
public crowdsourced database with episode-related

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.290
metadata that anyone can add information to.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.620
This would be useful for several different
reasons.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.510
We can, for instance, include implementation
links for each of the papers, for the ones

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:51.270
that have source code either from the authors
or some independent implementations from the

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.270
community.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.820
We can also include keywords on the topic
of the episode, such as machine learning,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:02.690
recurrent neural networks, cloth simulations
for an easy way to search for a topic of interest.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:07.580
If we are interested in any of these, we can
just easily search for a keyword and immediately

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.119
know what episode it was referenced in.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:15.310
The very same could be done with some of the
technical words used in the series, such as

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.350
Metropolis sampling, backpropagation and overfitting.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.229
This way, we could maybe build an intuitive
technical dictionary with definitions and

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:27.670
links pointing to the appropriate episodes
where they were explained.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.329
I think that would be the ultimate learning
resource and having such a dictionary would

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:36.990
be super useful - I was playing with the thought
of having this for quite a while now.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.320
So this data project has just started out
on the Two Minute Papers subreddit, but it

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.670
can only happen with the help of the community
- and this means you.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.960
If you're interested in helping, please drop
by and leave us a note, I've put a link in

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.310
the description box.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.200
Looking forward to seeing you there!

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.270
It seems that there is interest in doing such
collaborations and experiments together between

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.790
you Fellow Scholars.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:05.329
Imagine how cool it would be to see students
and researchers forming an open and helpful

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:10.410
community, brainstorming, running the implementations,
and sharing their ideas and findings with

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.410
each other.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:17.390
Who knows, maybe one day, a science paper
will be written as a result of such endeavors.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.720
Please let us know in the comments section
what you think about these things.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.910
Would you participate in such an endeavor?

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.540
As always, we love reading your awesome feedback!

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.160
Also, in the meantime, a huge thank you for
the following Fellow Scholars who translated

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.530
our episodes to several languages!

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:38.920
If you wish to contribute too, click the cogwheel
button in any video on the lower right, click

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.070
subtitles/CC, then add subtitles/CC.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:49.150
I am trying my very best to credit every contributor,
if I have forgotten anyone, that's not intended,

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.960
please let me know and I'll fix it.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.450
Meanwhile, on Patreon, we are currently oscillating
around our current milestone.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.680
Reaching this one means that all of our software
and hardware costs are covered, which is quite

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.680
amazing.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:07.210
Because creating YouTube videos with high
information density and short duration is

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:12.040
the very definition of financial suicide,
it's very helpful for us to have such a safety

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.290
net with Patreon.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.880
Also, there was an episode not so long ago
about the new Two Minute Papers machine which

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.290
was bought solely from your support, and I
am still stunned by this.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.560
I tried to explain this to close members of
the family that we were able to buy this new

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.790
machine with the support of complete strangers
from the internet whom I've never met.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.840
They said that this is clearly impossible.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:40.650
Apparently, it's not impossible - and so many
kind people are watching the series, really,

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.250
thank you so much!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.530
When we reach our milestone after that, we
will be able to spend 1% of these funds to

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.150
directly help other research projects and
conferences.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.430
Please remember that your support makes Two
Minute Papers possible, and you can cancel

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.390
these pledges at any time.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:02.090
Also, if you don't feel like using Patreon
or don't have any disposable income, that

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.570
is completely fine.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:08.310
I'd like to emphasize that none of this is
required, it's just an option to help, and

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.960
we completely understand that it's not easy
to make ends meet for many many of you, even

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.549
with lots of overtime at a tiring and difficult
job.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:21.539
Two Minute Papers is always going to be here
and will always be free for everyone.

00:04:21.539 --> 00:04:26.759
We would like to spread the word so even more
of us can marvel at the wonders of research.

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:31.110
Just watching the series and sharing these
episodes is also a great deal of help and

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.770
we are super grateful for it!

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:38.129
It is really incredible to see how the series
has grown and how many of you Fellow Scholars

00:04:38.129 --> 00:04:41.550
are interested in research, and the inventions
of the future.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.090
Let's continue our journey of science together!

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:49.780
In the meantime, Google DeepMind and Blizzard
has announced a joint effort to make it possible

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:55.120
for computer programs to play Starcraft 2,
a famous real-time strategy game from the

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.759
start of 2017.

00:04:56.759 --> 00:04:57.759
Whoa!

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:02.699
There was a question about the first thing
I will do when this project takes off.

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:08.810
Well, of course, I'll take one week of vacation
and write an AI that can play against itself

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.949
and watch with tremendous enjoyment as they
beat the living hell out of each other and

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:15.569
other real players.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:20.110
If I heard it correctly, in one of the upcoming
championships, computer algorithms will also

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:21.400
be allowed to play.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:27.130
And who knows, maybe defeat the reigning player
champions, you know, like in Chess and Go.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.439
We're living amazing times indeed.

00:05:29.439 --> 00:05:31.620
I am counting the days.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.669
Super excited.

00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:36.509
Thanks for watching, and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

